ssions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "  Describing Health Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">health problem</span> is a physical state when you do not feel well. It can cause you pain or discomfort. Sometimes a health problem can cause you not to function normally. It can make it hard for you to go to work or school, or do other things.<br /></br>You use the Present Continuous tense and the Simple Present tense to describe health problems:<br />   <span class=\"italic\">I'm not feeling well.<br /> I feel \u2026<br /> I have a \u2026<span />"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Andy</span> : How are you?<br /> <span class =\"strong\">Joe</span> : I'm not feeling well. (Subject + To Be + V-ing)<br /> <span class =\"strong\">Andy</span> : What's wrong?<br /> <span class =\"strong\">Joe</span> : I have a headache. (Subject + Simple Present Tense)<br />"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Modals Should and Must"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal <span class =\"strong\">should</span>  to give recommendations or advice about health problems.<br /> The modal <span class =\"strong\">must</span>   shows necessity or obligation. You use it to give very strong advice about health problems."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class =\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Recommendation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  You should get some rest.   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Necessity\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  You must go to the doctor.   </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stomach ache "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pain in a person's stomach "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a stomach ache."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about being sick."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "headache "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a pain in a person's head "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a headache."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sore throat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pain in someone's throat "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't talk ... I have a sore throat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "runny nose "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "excess liquid from someone's nose, usually when they're sick "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a runny nose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sick "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "affected by physical illness; unwell "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I feel sick. I can't go to work today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "contagious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something can be passed from person to person through contact "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The sickness is contagious. Be careful!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "timesheet "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at a job, the chart with the hours a person works "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Please fill in the timesheet for next week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to update "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give the newest information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Please update your timesheet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le03ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you are an employee and your partner is your manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short dialogue (8-10 lines) describing some health problems you have."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask for time off. Your boss gives you some strong advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice the dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Switch roles, and practice again."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I describe health problems in complete statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a polite request to my boss."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give strong advice to an employee."}]}], "type": "sena"}